--- body ---
## Context

The 2025-q1 workbook of the South African JET Grants Register carries a
footnote "Green Highlight: Indicates that…", so a cell fill carries
meaning the publisher states. The v1 XLSX adapter of [[1950]]
(`scripts/jetp/_xlsx_cells.py`) reads cell values only: the footnote is
admitted as a heading statement, but the highlighted rows are not marked.

## Method

- Read the fill of each cell from the workbook styles (`xl/styles.xml`
  fills, the cell's style index), standard library only, as the v1 adapter
  does.
- Record the fill on the row's line as a verbatim field (colour as stored,
  plus the legend text that gives it meaning when the edition prints one),
  under a new parser method version; editions re-read by replay
  (extraction § 10).
- Check the other workbook edition (2024-q3) for fills with or without a
  legend, and report them.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Fill read per cell and recorded per row as a verbatim field, with
  the legend text where printed
- [x] Red test: a fixture row with and without the legend fill
- [x] New method version; the 2025-q1 lines superseded by replay, counts
  unchanged
- [x] `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
